<Layout title="City of Trove — the novel | Trove Collections">
  <section class="novel-hero">
    <p class="kicker">FROM TROVE COLLECTIONS PRESS · COMING AT THE END OF 2026</p>
    <h1>CITY OF TROVE</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">An Archaeological Adventure Thriller · Book One · by Micki Sharp</p>
  </section>

  <section class="boundary">
    <p><em>A word about this page. Everything else on this site is real — the pearls, the hangar,
    the hundred years of family flying, every item in every collection. This is the one thing we
    made up. We think you'll like it anyway.</em></p>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section class="blurb">
    <p><strong>He spent forty-one years being told what was wrong with him. Nobody ever guessed
    the truth: he was built for a different world.</strong></p>
    <p>Roan Wells captains a private Boeing 787 for an owner he has never met. He holds a spotless
    record, a house on a desert mesa he chose without knowing why, and a lifetime of small
    wrongnesses he has learned to hide — the memory that forgets nothing, the languages that come
    too easily, the airport magnetometers that trip when he walks through clean.</p>
    <p>Then a salvage crew raises an impossible stone from a mountain crypt, a beam of aquamarine
    light stands straight up out of a sleeping Andean volcano, and the quiet arrangement that has
    steered Roan's entire life begins calling in its debts. At the bottom of Lake Titicaca there
    is a door. Behind the door is a city that has been waiting twelve thousand years — and it
    knows his name.</p>
    <p>But Roan is not the only one who kept the old appointment. An order of seven ancient houses
    has watched the world's waters for four hundred generations, and its patience has curdled into
    a hunt. Something else has been waiting too — behind a deeper door, in the dark below the city,
    pressing at a crack only it can feel.</p>
    <p><strong>The watch is ending. The heir has come home.</strong></p>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section class="why">
    <h2>What inspired this book</h2>
    <p>The author's grandfather soloed a Velie Monocoupe in 1928. Four generations later the family
    is still flying — three airline captains in the line, a century in the air, and a habit of
    saying the important words out loud so the next generation carries them before they understand
    them. <em>City of Trove</em> is about a four-hundred-generation watch. The four-generation
    version is documented on our <a href="/heritage">Heritage</a> page — that part is all true.</p>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section class="cta">
    <h2>Start reading now</h2>
    <p><a class="button" href="/novel/chapter-one">Read Chapter One free →</a></p>
    <p>Or get <a href="/novel/portfolio">The Trove Portfolio</a> — the free illustrated
    companion: two dozen full-page paintings from the making of the book — and be first to hear
    when the doors open.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>

